    {
      "id": "ab3253303541093fc3c725fd5cd3ddd74cb57b04",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 967066280,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I am all for giving classes special meaning, but the main reason here is, that there was a QString provided as pointer (which it shouldn’t be in the first place) and not freed properly. For me, this change seems to go in the wrong direction. Don’t get me wrong, I long wanted a cleaner solution to this dialog, but this makes it harder to change stuff in the future and duplicates code. I would rather investigate why the QString is required to be a pointer and change that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-06-01T04:38:36.680Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-06-01T04:39:24.603Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 158203477,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2022-06-02T12:30:35.318Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7050,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 967263465,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "After some investigation, there is a much simpler solution to the issue here. Just make the filter QString a non-referenced QString, and provide a getter method for the dialog to return the stored displayFilter. That way, the original QString is given by copy and you can use open_dlg.displayFilter() to request the filter. This also makes it a little bit clearer, that the filter can actually be manipulated by the dialog as in contrast to the current solution, where the manipulation is not so easily seen.\n\nIts 10-lines for the CaptureFileDialog class, and then the call to the dialog instead of using the original variable in the calling methods. Much easier change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-06-01T07:41:55.513Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-06-01T07:42:12.911Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 158203477,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2022-06-02T12:30:35.318Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7050,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 968534824,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, that might be the best solution.\n\nI considered making the QString a pointer instead of a reference, so it wouldn't have to be instantiated, and then just dealing with a possibly null filter string if the open or merge routines were called, but I thought that was even worse, with a single class with two methods that couldn't be called if it was instantiated a particular way.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-06-01T23:45:00.736Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-06-01T23:45:00.736Z",
